    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Approximately 12,000 new spinal cord injuries (SCI) occur in the US each year, and less than 1% of SCI patients have full neurological recovery. Current treatments for SCI are limited to reducing inflammation and preventing further degradation. As such, developing a regenerative therapy for SCI would be transformational. The cellular transplantation of olfactory ensheathing glia (OEG) has been shown to be a potential solution, but developing an efficient cell-delivery and engraftment mechanism for transplantation remains a significant challenge. Previous studies have suggested that cell delivery within a carrier gel may increase cell viability, but a majority of these gels suffer from critical limitations that prevent their translation to clinical use. A recently developed family of hydrogels called Sheer-thinning Hydrogel for Injectable Encapsulation and Long-term Delivery (SHIELD) that are biocompatible, customizable, and reproducible may provide a more translatable and optimized solution to enhance transplantation for SCI repair. Here we assay in vitro the behavior of OEGs encapsulated in SHIELD and demonstrate that these hydrogels are capable of protecting and supporting the OEGs. Metabolic activity and cell death assays along with fluorescence immunocytochemistry show that the cells are healthier when encapsulated within SHIELD compared to cell-only controls. OEG delivery in vivo was also shown to be enhanced when encapsulated with SHIELD. These results suggest that encapsulating OEGs in the hydrogel prior to transplantation is an attractive strategy to increase the efficacy of cellular transplantations and may serve to significantly increase functional regeneration in SCI repair. In the future, SHIELD may increase the efficacy of a variety of cell-based therapies.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
